    "name": "Card'em All!",
    "steam_appid": 3520540,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3520540/extras/48bb2b4a964daad900f284ed9a379a3a.avif?t=1743631184\" width=462 height=174 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Card'em All!</strong> is a rogue-like deck-builder with a twist, incorporating the following rules and features:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you face a wave of enemies, you can do the following:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use your natural attack, as permitted</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play cards that represent Units, Abilities, or Effects</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Units, once deployed, act on their own and use their own attacks and abilities</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you have no units in front, enemy attacks affect you and your health pool.</p></li></ul></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Several Waves comprise an Encounter.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your units persist across waves, until the end of an Encounter.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies drop loot in the form of Booty, the fate of which is decided at the end of an Encounter.</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At the end of each Encounter you are offered one or more choices for a reward.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >These rewards often include cards for your deck.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Certain cards have upkeep and require special attention.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Booty is added to your Gold pool.</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A series of Encounters comprises a Run. Different Runs, across timelines, bring you closer to waking up from the dream sequence and winning the game.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > When you die, your dream sequence starts from the beginning with the following changes:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You retain all your deck</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You retain half of your gold</p></li></ul></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Vision for the game:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Card'em All</strong> is in an early stage of development. At the moment, the plan is to have two modes of play: a linear campaign with a beginning and an end and a card-hunting/collecting mode to be played separately.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Release plan:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Subject to change the plan is to release <strong>Card'em All</strong> in the last quarter of 2025.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3520540/extras/48bb2b4a964daad900f284ed9a379a3a.avif?t=1743631184\" width=462 height=174 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Card'em All!</strong> is a rogue-like deck-builder with a twist, incorporating the following rules and features:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you face a wave of enemies, you can do the following:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use your natural attack, as permitted</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play cards that represent Units, Abilities, or Effects</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Units, once deployed, act on their own and use their own attacks and abilities</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you have no units in front, enemy attacks affect you and your health pool.</p></li></ul></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Several Waves comprise an Encounter.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your units persist across waves, until the end of an Encounter.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies drop loot in the form of Booty, the fate of which is decided at the end of an Encounter.</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At the end of each Encounter you are offered one or more choices for a reward.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >These rewards often include cards for your deck.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Certain cards have upkeep and require special attention.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Booty is added to your Gold pool.</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A series of Encounters comprises a Run. Different Runs, across timelines, bring you closer to waking up from the dream sequence and winning the game.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > When you die, your dream sequence starts from the beginning with the following changes:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You retain all your deck</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You retain half of your gold</p></li></ul></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Vision for the game:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Card'em All</strong> is in an early stage of development. At the moment, the plan is to have two modes of play: a linear campaign with a beginning and an end and a card-hunting/collecting mode to be played separately.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Release plan:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Subject to change the plan is to release <strong>Card'em All</strong> in the last quarter of 2025.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "short_description": "Trapped in ages-long slumber, fight trough timelines of nightmares to defeat your fears and assemble a mighty deck to face your ultimate challenge and finally awake! Surviving through each defeat, your deck grows stronger and stronger, bringing you one step closer to victory.",
